<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bangladesh Liberation War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1971</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Bangladesh Liberation War was the conflict of 1971 in which <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-pakistan">East Pakistan</a> won independence as Bangladesh. After the Pakistani army began a crackdown in March 1971, Bengali nationalist forces, the Mukti Bahini, fought a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guerrilla-warfare">guerrilla</a> war and some ten million refugees fled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. India intervened in December, and on 16 December about 93,000 Pakistani troops surrendered in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dhaka">Dhaka</a>. Hundreds of thousands of people were killed.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bangladesh-liberation-war.jpg" alt="Bangladesh Liberation War" width="320" height="211" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: ExcelD24 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:BangladeshLiberationWarMontage.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
